# Conventional Commits

Use [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/) for every commit message.

## Format

```
<type>(<optional scope>): <short description>
```

- **type**: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `test`, `chore`, `ci`, `build`, `perf`
- **scope**: optional area (e.g. `frontend`, `api`, `deps`)
- **description**: imperative mood, lowercase, no trailing period

## Examples

- `feat(frontend): add ArticlesIndexPage component`
- `fix(views): load application.tsx vite entrypoint`
- `test(system): update dismiss tests for React articles index`
- `ci: build Vite test assets before test jobs`
- `chore(deps): add react-router-dom`

## When committing

- One logical change per commit; split by file when each file is a distinct concern.
- Prefer `feat` for user-facing behavior, `fix` for bugs, `test` for test-only changes.
